%I A401906 #18 Nov 16 2026 17:56:52
%S A401906 11,19,22,23,25,38,39,43,44,46,47,50,53,55,59,67,71,76,78,79,83,86,87,
%T A401906 88,89,92,94,95,97,100,103,106,109,110,111,113,115,118,121,123,131,
%U A401906 134,137,139,142,143,145,151,152,156,158,159,166,167,172,174,175,176,177,178,179,183,184,187,188,190
%N A401906 Numbers not of the form abs(k - reversal of k in base 2) for at least one k (written in base 10).
%C A401906 The search space is finite since if m has N binary digits, then we only need to search for k with at most 2*N binary digits.
%C A401906 Leading 0's are disregarded in reversals: reverse(10_2) = 1_2 and reverse(100100_2) = 1001_2.
%C A401906 If m appears in this sequence then so does 2*m: if m odd then there exists k - reversal(k) = m and k = (d_N...d_0)_2 if and only if k' = (1 d_N...d_0 1)_2, k' - reversal(k') = 2*m (repeat by induction on powers of 2 dividing m).
%H A401906 Adam Onus, <a href="/A401906/b401906.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..24159</a>
%H A401906 Adam Onus, <a href="/A401906/a401906_1.py.txt">Python program</a>
%Y A401906 Complement of A400463.
%Y A401906 Cf. A030101, A055945, A335978
%K A401906 nonn,base,new
%O A401906 1,1
%A A401906 _Adam Onus_, Nov 09 2026
